  "name": "Inequalities with Two Logarithms",
  "problem": "When we have two logarithms in an inequality, we can use the same solution procedure as before: we use each side of the inequality as an exponent of the base of the logarithm.\n\nJust remember that we still need to remove extraneous solutions. We can do this by keeping only the solutions that are in the domains of *all* the logarithms in the original inequality.",
